Quail measurement corpus — license
===================================

This license covers only the contents of this `data/quail/` subtree: the generated
documents underlying the compiled corpus fragments, the compiled corpus fragments
themselves (`corpus/`), the fact and probe lists (`corpus/en-preliminary/`), the trained
n-gram overlay files (`overlays/`), the descent configuration (`config/`), and the
measurement results (`results/`). It does not cover the rest of this repository (see the
repository root LICENSE and NOTICE for the code license).

These are our own contributions: text and question/answer fragments generated from a
private "bible" we wrote, plus overlays and measurements we produced by running our own
technique against them. They are licensed to you under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0):

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

In short: you may copy, redistribute, and adapt this material for any purpose, including
commercially, as long as you give appropriate credit, provide a link to the license, and
indicate if changes were made.

No rights are granted, waived, or implied over the work that inspired this corpus. This
corpus is inspired from memory by Philip K. Dick's short story *We Can Remember It for You
Wholesale* (1966); no text of the original work is included, and this license grants
nothing with respect to that original work or any rights its own copyright holders may
have. See PROVENANCE.md for the full statement.
